  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is an 81\u2011year\u2011old male with a long history of cardiovascular, metabolic, and renal disease. Over the past decades he progressed from hypertension and type\u20112 diabetes to chronic kidney disease (now stage\u202f4) and anemia. In early 2003 he was diagnosed with stage\u202f1 non\u2011small cell lung cancer, received cisplatin and paclitaxel, and remains under oncologic surveillance. Atrial fibrillation was identified in late 2003 and is being managed with rate\u2011control agents and warfarin. He is awaiting kidney transplantation. He also has obstructive sleep apnea, obesity, hypertriglyceridemia, and diabetic retinopathy. Socially, he reports housing instability, limited social contact, social isolation, a criminal record, and part\u2011time employment, which may affect adherence. Recent visits (up to Dec\u202f2003) focus on chronic disease management, medication review, and cancer follow\u2011up.",
